# Batch E: when .npmignore exists, npm does NOT consult .gitignore, so this
# file must carry every exclusion that matters for the published tarball.
#
# The built Linux native helper binary + trust manifest are gitignored build
# artifacts, but they MUST ship in the tarball: without them an installed
# consumer cannot use anchored filesystem operations and fails closed.
# They ship because package.json "files" lists scripts/, and entries in
# "files" cannot be excluded by .gitignore. The negations below state that
# inclusion explicitly, so a future change to the "files" list cannot
# silently drop them.
!scripts/native/vcp-linux-fsops
!scripts/native/vcp-linux-fsops.manifest.json

# NEVER ship Windows candidate artifacts. The Windows native helper is a
# separate, D-01-gated, unshipped candidate; a Linux tarball must not carry
# a Windows executable, and a Linux binary must never satisfy Windows.
scripts/native/vcp-windows-fsops.exe
scripts/native/vcp-windows-fsops.obj
build/

# Local/editor artefacts (mirrors .gitignore for packed directories).
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.tmp
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
